TITLE:: PatternChip
SUMMARY:: Labelled chip for one sequence in the Arranger.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views
RELATED:: Classes/Arranger, Classes/BorderView, Classes/Sequencer

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PatternChip:: is a LINK::Classes/BorderView:: that LINK::Classes/Arranger:: places for each sequence. It stores that sequence's LINK::Classes/Symbol:: id, the same id LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: uses, and shows it as a centred LINK::Classes/StaticText::. The chip uses LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: colour3 as its fill and LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-extreme2:: as its border colour. The border width starts at 0. A left double-click calls LINK::Classes/Sequencer#-play:: with that id and looping on, and sets this chip's border width to 2. Double-clicking the chip that is playing calls LINK::Classes/Sequencer#-stop:: and sets the border width to 0. Double-clicking a different chip moves the border to that chip.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::PatternChip:: and adds it to CODE::parent::.

ARGUMENT:: parent
The LINK::Classes/View:: that holds the chip.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: that plays this chip's sequence.

ARGUMENT:: sequenceId
The LINK::Classes/Symbol:: that identifies the sequence, displayed with CODE::asString::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::PatternChip:: instance.

PRIVATE:: prInit, prTogglePlay
